From 224d320e3ff73bdfe73cf48e8eacfb40c259eff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:12:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-broker: a submission's marker is optional, so RADV's
 GPU-clock read goes through

The broker refused every submission without a client marker (argument[0]), though it never uses the marker: it
fences with its own page, and the client's own words write its marker. RADV's GPU-clock read
(radv_ps5_read_gpu_clock) submits its timestamp packet with none, so in every broker client each timestamp and clock
calibration read 0 (RADEON_TIMESTAMP, vkGetCalibratedTimestampsKHR, D3D12 GetClockCalibration), and the broker's log
showed operation=4 status=0x16 for each read.

- server.cpp submit(): a marker that is given must still be the client's and 4-byte aligned; none is no longer
  EINVAL.

Proven: server.cpp compiles with the title's own command. PS5_Proton's tests/d3d12-clock-probe.c (non-zero, rising
GPU readings at the CPU's rate) is the console check. Not yet run on a console; a side branch on the pinned
ace98a99 for that run, not main.
---
 tooling/gpu-broker/server.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tooling/gpu-broker/server.cpp b/tooling/gpu-broker/server.cpp
index 468bb18..6f4f0cf 100644
--- a/tooling/gpu-broker/server.cpp
+++ b/tooling/gpu-broker/server.cpp
@@ -689,8 +689,12 @@ void free_buffer(Client &c,Buffer &b,FILE *out)
 }
 int submit(Client &c,const PwGpuMessage &m,FILE *out,unsigned client)
 {
+    // The client's marker is optional: the broker fences with its own page (Fences), and the client's words write
+    // its marker themselves. RADV's GPU-clock read (radv_ps5_read_gpu_clock) sends none and was refused, so every
+    // timestamp and clock calibration a broker client asked for read 0. A marker that is given must still be the
+    // client's.
     if(!m.bytes || m.bytes%4 || m.bytes>16*1024*1024 || m.address%4 || !owned(c,m.address,m.bytes) ||
-       !m.argument[0] || m.argument[0]%4 || !owned(c,m.argument[0],4))return EINVAL;
+       (m.argument[0] && (m.argument[0]%4 || !owned(c,m.argument[0],4))))return EINVAL;
     if(wedged)return EIO;
     if(!fences_ready(out))return ENOMEM;
     const uint64_t t0=radv_ps5_now_ns();
